It's easy to make a multiplayer game balanced like that: Eliminate all
random events, give each player the same options and starting point[1],
voila. All this tells us is that the concept of balance applied to
multiplayer games is a different one from that applied to single player
computer games.

[1] In chess, white gets the first move, so theoretically in a game with
two perfect players, white should always win, making it imbalanced.
Practically the game is complex enough to make this negligible.

